// A REST inside a grace body — the one grob general-grace-settings never names.
//
// LILYPOND-REF: scm/music-functions.scm:636-650 general-grace-settings (v2.26.0) gives a
// font-size to Stem, Flag, NoteHead, TabNoteHead, Dots, Accidental, Script, Fingering and
// StringNumber, and NEVER to Rest — so a grace rest reads the STAFF's own size. MEASURED
// side by side in one book (scratch/p308/lp2/s2_gracerestchord, `\grace { r16 d'16 }`):
// LilyPond draws the rest at 0.0040 and the head beside it at 0.0028 = magstep(-3), and the
// rest's path data is BYTE-IDENTICAL to a main-stream rest's.
//
// ⚠️ WHY THIS BOOK EXISTS. Session 308 taught the model that a grace column can hold no
// head, and got the SIZE right — the rest was drawn at the staff's FontSize. What nothing
// watched was the FACE: the grace pass drew it inside the grace group's
// MusicFace(Emmentaler-14) scope, so a full-size glyph came out of the FOURTEEN design's
// outline, which is not the outline a main-stream rest has (Emmentaler is optically sized).
// Session 313 measured that the whole disk — 1418 .lys, tracked and untracked — held NOT ONE
// book with a rest in a grace body, so no snapshot and no ledger point could have said so.
// This is that book. The third bar is the dotted case, whose augmentation dot rides the
// rest's own origin.
title "Grace rest"

time 4/4
key c major

part melody

phrase graceLeadingRest {
  // A rest at the FRONT of the run: LilyPond beams nothing at all here, because the
  // beam covers the leading run of HEAD columns and there is none.
  grace { r16 d16 } c4 c2. |
}

phrase graceInnerRest {
  // A rest INSIDE the run: the leading two heads carry the beam, the rest breaks it, and
  // the head after it takes a flag (scratch/p308/lp2/measurements.md).
  grace { d16 e16 r16 f16 } c4 c2. |
}

phrase graceDottedRest {
  grace { r8. d16 } c4 c2. |
}

section Main {
  melody { graceLeadingRest graceInnerRest graceDottedRest }
}

form main { Main }

score main "grace-rest" {
  staff melody
}
